The module-level strict transform over an arbitrary, possibly non-Noetherian, base is missing. Narrower versions are planned elsewhere:
- Tau Ceti StableReduction layer 4 ('exceptional divisor, strict transform', beside its general blowup);
- AlgebraicModuliForArithmeticGeometry R09.7a (strict, total and controlled transforms for characteristic-zero varieties);
- AdicCoefficientsAndComparisons L5 (strict transforms for de Jong's alterations);
- AdicSpacesPartII R2/admissible-blow-up (the formal strict transform of coherent modules, Raynaud–Gruson 5.1.1).
The owner imports the scheme-level construction from StableReduction layer 4. It adds only the module version, with the properties flattening uses: Stacks 080E (identification with the blowup of f^{-1}Z), 080G (Lemma 31.34.4, commuting with affine pushforward) and Lemma 31.34.7 (exact sequences with a universally injective free submodule).
